$DATUM 78-67-1
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure 2: To a flask were added
phthalide (6 mmol), NBS (7.2 mmol), and AIBN (0.6 mmol) under an argon
atmo-sphere. The mixture was well mixed with stirring for 2 min. Then the
mixture was heated at 60 °C until the starting phthalide was consumed
completely. After one hour, diethyl ether (15 mL) was added to the
mixture, and the obtained mixture was filtered to re-move succinimide.
The filtrate was evaporated and the residue was chromatographed on silica
gel (eluent: hexane-ethyl acetate = 1:1) to give 3-bromophthalide. Yield
75%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry-solvent, regioselective, Wohl-Ziegler reaction, reaction
alternately run with benzoyl peroxide as catalyst or using [bmim]PF6
ionic solvent with comparable yields
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Environmentally-friendly Wohl-Ziegler bromination: Ionic-liquid reaction
and solvent-free reaction
