$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1,2-Dibromo-1-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)alkanes
4a,b and 3-Bromo-1-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)alk-1-enes 4c,d; General
Procedure. A soln of 3a-d (10.8 mmol) in n-hexane or pentane (50 mL) was
stirred with Br2 (13 mmol) at r.t. for 12 h. Volatiles were removed and
the crude products were purified by chromatography (silica gel, n-hexane
or pentane) giving pure 4a-d (Schemes 4 and 5).
[(3E)-2-Bromo-4-(pentafluoro-λ6-sulfanyl)but-3-enyl]benzene as a
colorless oil, yield 75%. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 7.28-7.48 (m, 5 H,
Ph), 6.47 (m, J = 6.0 Hz, 1 H, SF5CH=CH), 6.40-6.52 (m, 1 H, SF5CH), 4.98
(dd, J = 8.7, 6.0 Hz, 1 H, BrCH), 3.03-3.40 (m, 1 HB, CH2), 2.94-3.03 (m,
1 HA, CH2). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 143.0 (quint, J = 20.1 Hz,
HCSF5), 140.4 (Ph), 135.0 (quint, J = 7.7 Hz, HC=CHSF5), 129.0 (Ph),
127.2 (Ph), 51.4 (CHBr), 40.8 (CH2). 19F NMR (376 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 83.1
(9 lines, A-part), 62.6 (dm, J = 148.7 Hz, B4-part). MS (EI): m/z (%) =
257 (32) [M - SF5]+, 256 (35) [M - HSF5]+, 130 (30) [M - BrSF5]+, 129
(100) [M - HBr - SF5]+. Anal. Calcd for C10H10BrF5S: C, 35.62; H, 2.99;
Br, 23.70; S, 9.51. Found: C, 35.59; H, 2.97; Br, 23.45; S, 9.53.
