$DATUM 3-(1-Bromo-2-carboxy)ethyl-4-methyl-2,5-furandione (9). A mixture of acid
7 (552 mg, 3 mmol), NBS (2.67 g, 15 mmol), and a catalytic amount of
benzoyl peroxide (30 mg) in CHCl3 (40 mL) was gently refluxed for 24 h.
The reaction mixture was allowed to cool to r.t. and was concentrated in
vacuo. The residue was purified by silica gel column chromatography
(petroleum ether-EtOAc, 1:3) to obtain pure bromo acid 9. Waxy solid,
yield (584 mg, 74%). IR (nujol): ν = 1828, 1778, 1722 cm-1. 1H NMR (200
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 2.20 (s, 3H), 3.40 (dd, J = 12 and 4 Hz, 1H), 3.58 (dd,
J = 12 and 6 Hz, 1H), 5.15 (t, J = 6 Hz, 1H). 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ
= 9.8, 31.7, 39.9, 140.3, 142.6, 162.9, 164.7, 174.1. MS m/z: 264, 262,
246, 244, 218, 216, 183, 165, 139, 111, 93, 82, 64, 55. Anal. Calcd for
C8H7BrO5 (263.1): C, 36.52; H, 2.68. Found: C, 36.32; H, 2.84.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM A facile synthesis of a (±)-2,3-disubstituted maleic anhydride segment of
tautomycin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Deshpande, Anil M.; Natu, Arvind A.; Argade, Narshinha P.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2001), (5), 702-704

