$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 4.5.6. Bromination of sultones 2e and 2f
(general procedure 5) Sultone 2e or 2f (0.1 mmol) was dissolved in CHCl3
(15 mL). NBS (0.019 g, 0.105 mmol) was added, and the reaction mixturewas
stirred at rt. After 1 h, the volatiles were removed in vacuo. The
residue was dissolved in ethyl acetate and filtered through a 2-cm silica
gel layer. The solvent was removed in vacuo, and the products were
purified by column chromatography with pentane/ethyl acetate (3:1).
4.5.7. 3-Bromo-4,6-di(4-methoxyphenyl)-[1,2]-oxathiine 2,2-dioxide (8e)
4.5.8. 3-Bromo-4,6-di(2-methoxyphenyl)-[1,2]-oxathiine 2,2-dioxide (8f)
Yield: 70%. Pale yellow solid. m.p. 142-143ºC. Rf = 0.35 (pentane/ethyl
acetate, 3:1). 1H NMR: 3.97 (s, 6H), 7.00 (s, 1H), 7.05-7.17 (m, 4H),
7.36-7.40 (m, 1H), 7.49-7.58 (m, 2H), 7.92 (dd, J = 7.9 and 1.7 Hz, 1H).
13C NMR: 55.62 (CH3), 55.65 (CH3), 110.08 (C), 111.21 (CH), 111.42 (CH),
111.48 (CH), 119.19 (C), 120.64 (CH), 120.89 (CH), 125.53 (C), 128.63
(CH), 129.51 (CH), 131.06 (CH), 132.02 (CH), 144.75 (C), 150.07 (C),
156.09 (C), 157.47 (C). MS (ESI): 423 [M+H]+, 440 [M+NH4]+, 864
[2M+NH4]+. IR: 528, 574, 612, 652, 683, 747, 784, 806, 835, 852, 896,
956, 1008, 1045, 1084, 1122, 1186, 1245, 1289, 1370, 1433, 1458, 1473,
1490, 1529, 1611, 1632, 1729, 2839, 2966, 3015, 3117. Elemental analysis:
calc. for C18H15BrO5S: C 51.08, H 3.57, S 7.58; found: 50.89, H 3.32, S
7.32.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Simple and practical one-step synthesis of new 1,3-diene δ-sultones from
terminal alkynes and some synthetic applications of these compounds
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Gaitzsch, Jens; Rogachev, Victor; Metz, Peter; Filimonov, Victor D.;
Zahel, Martin; Kataeva, Olga
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Sulfur Chemistry (2011), 32(1), 3-16

