$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination with N-Bromosuccinimide/K-10; α-Bromo β-Enamino Ketones 2a-g,
4a and α-Bromo β-Enamino Ester 4b; General Procedure N-Bromosuccinimide
(3.5 mmol) was suspended in MeOH (6 mL) and added to
3-amino-5,5-dimethylcyclohex-2-en-1-one 1a-g, 4-amino penten-2-one 4a or
ethyl 3-amino butenoate 3b (3 mmol) dispersed on K-10 (0.9 g; Fluka). The
mixture was stirred at r.t. for 5 h. After completion of the reactions
(TLC/CH2Cl2), the products were extracted by washing the K-10 with CH2Cl2
(4 10 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with sat. NaHCO3 (13
mL), dried (MgSO4), filtered, and the solvent was removed under vacuum to
yield the crude products. Solid compounds were recrystallized from
diisopropyl ether. Compound 2d was purified by column chromatography on
silica gel (Aldrich, 230-400 mesh) using EtOAc-CH2Cl2 (1:1). Yields and
NMR data are repoorted in the table. Compound 2c, yield 74%. Mp(°C):
90-92; 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm), J (Hz): 1.10 (s, 6 H), 1.28 (d, 6
H, J = 6.4), 2.39 (s, 2 H), 2.44 (s, 2 H), 3.77 (m, 1 H), 5.52 (br, 1 H);
13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm): 24.03, 28.18, 32.10, 40.15, 45.11,
50.34, 94.37, 158.40, 186.83.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM montmorillonite K-10 catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM α-Bromination of β-enamino compounds using K-10
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Braibante, Mara E. F.; Braibante, Hugo T. S.; Rosso, Giovanni B.; Da
Roza, Juliano K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2001), (13), 1935-1937

