$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of derivatives of
5-alkylfuran-2-carboxylic acides (general procedure). A mixture of 0.01
mol of alkylfuran, 0.0105 mol of N-bromosuccinimide, and 0.05 g of
azodiisobutyronitrile was boiled with stirring for 1.5-2 h until traces
of N-bromosuccinimide disappeared. The reaction mixture was left
overnight. The succinimide was then filtered off, washed with carbon
tetrachloride, and the solvent was removed at reduced pressure. The
brominated esters were kept at room temperature in a vacuum (2 mm), while
the nitriles were distilled in a vacuum.
5-(1-Bromo-2-methylpropyl)-2-cyanofuran (VIII). Yield 74%. bp 99°C (1 mm
Hg). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 0.94 d (isobutyl CH3, JHH 7 Hz); 1.13d
(isobutyl CH3, JHH 7 Hz); 2.35 m (isobutyl CH, JHH 7 Hz); 4.73 d (CHBr.
JHH 7 Hz); 6.43 s (furan H4); 7.04 s (furan H3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and phosphorylation of 5-bromoalkyl derivatives of
2-furancarboxylic acid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pevzner, L. M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of General Chemistry (2005), 75(2), 230-233

