$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of compounds I and IV with a
solution of bromine in dimethylformamide (general procedure). A solution
of an equimolar amount of bromine in 5 ml of DMF was added dropwise over
a period of 15 min to a solution of 0.24 mol of compound Ia or IVa or
0.33 mol of Ib or IVb in 5 ml of DMF under stirring at room temperature.
The mixture was stirred for 1 h, an additional 1 equiv of bromine in DMF
was added and the mixture was stirred until the initial compound
disappeared according to the TLC data. The mixture was then diluted with
two volumes of water and the red (compounds II) or violet (V) precipitate
was filtered off, washed with water and dried. The products were purified
by preparative thin layer chromatography (II) or by heating in boiling
acetone-hexane (1 : 10) over a period of 30 min to remove impurities (V).
9-Bromo-4,4a-tetramethylene-1,3-diphenyl-3,4,4a,8-tetrahydropyrido[1,2-a]benzimidazol-8-one
(IIa).
(2-Bromo-4,4a-tetramethylene-1,3-diphenyl-3,4,4a,8-tetrahydropyrido[1,2-a]benzimidazol-8-ylidene)
malononitrile (Va). Yield 72%. mp 251-253 °C. 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm:
1.50-2.40 m (9H), 3.96 d (1H, 3-H, J = 9.9 Hz), 4.85 d (1H, 9-H, J = 1.7
Hz), 7.07 d (1H, 6-H, J = 9.6 Hz), 7.37 d.d (1H, 8-H, J = 9.6, 1.7 Hz),
7.20-7.60 m (10H, C6H5). Found, %: C 69.84; H 4.79; N 10.66. Mass
spectrum: m/z 519 [M + H]+. C30H23BrN4. Calculated, %: C 69.37; H 4.46; N
10.79. M 519.43.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, incremental addition of bromine and DMF
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Selective monobromination in the series of quinoid
pyrido[1,2-a]benzimidazole derivatives
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Slabko, O. Yu.; Tyshchenko, I. N.; Kaminskii, V. A.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Russian Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 45(3), 460-462

