$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Synthesis of
7,7-Dimethyl-2,4-dibromo-6-trimethylsilyldithieno[2,3-b:4'3'-d]silole (8)
from 1. NBS (3.40 g, 19.1 mmol, 2.0 equiv) was added into a solution of 1
(3.50 g, 9.54 mmol) in chloroform/AcOH (60 mL, 3:1, v/v) at ambient
temperature. The reaction mixture was heated to 60 °C for 6 h and then
quenched with water at ambient temperature.The reaction mixture was
heated to 60 °C for 6 h and then quenched with water at ambient
temperature. The workup was same as that for the synthesis of 6.
Synthesis of
7,7-Dimethyl-2,4-dibromo-6-trimethylsilyldithieno[2,3-b:4'3'-d]silole (8)
from 2. The procedure of making 8 from 2 is the same to that for the
synthesis of 8 from 1. From the reaction on the 265 mg scale of 2, 197 mg
(72.1%) of 8 was obtained. Mp: 70-72 °C. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ
7.87(s, 1 H), 0.50(s, 6 H), 0.35 (s, 9 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3): δ
151.9, 149.7, 149.3, 146.8, 142.5, 125.3, 120.5, 105.9, 0.4, -1.0. IR
(KBr): 2952.3, 2895.4 (C-H) cm-1. HRMS (TFMS ESI): m/z [M + H]+ calcd for
C13H17Br2S2Si2 450.8672, found 450.8676 [C13H1779Br2S2Si2], 452.8654
[C13H1779Br81Br S2Si2], and 454.8630 [C13H1781Br2S2Si2]. Formula weight:
452.38; Crystal system, space group: Monoclinic, P2(1)/c; Unit cell
dimensions: a =9.575(3) Å α= 90 °; b = 19.537(5) Å β= 109.511(3) °; c =
10.714(3) Å γ= 90 °; Volume = 1889.1(8) Å 3; Z, Calculated density: 4,
1.591 Mg/m3; Crystal size: 0.35 x 0.29 x 0.17 mm3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Dithieno[2,3-b:4',3'-d]siloles and Their Selective
Bromination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
