$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for the synthesis of
(E/Z)-(1-bromo-3-fluorobut-2-en-2-yl)(phenyl)sulfane and
(E/Z)-(1,4-dibromo-3-fluorobut-2-en-2-yl)(phenyl)sulfane: In a two necked
50 ml round bottom flask fitted with condenser, 0.5g (2.7mmol) of
(E/Z)-(3-fluorobut-2-en-2-yl)(phenyl)sulfane, N-bromosuccinamide (0.98g,
5.5mmol) and AIBN (cata lytical) were dissolved in 50 ml of Benzene. The
reaction mixture was refluxed for four hours. After the completion of the
reaction (monitored by TLC), cooled the reaction mixture, filtered
through sintered glass funnel, concentrated the filtrate under vacuo to
get crude product. The residue was purified by silica gel column
chromatography using hexane as eluent to give 5, 6 and 7 as yellow
colored liquid. Spectral data
(E/Z)-(1,4-dibromo-3-fluorobut-2-en-2-yl)(phenyl)sulfane (6): Yellowish
oil; 72% yield. 1H NMR (400MHz, CDCl3): δ 4.04 (2H, d, J = 2.0 Hz, CH2),
4.39 (2H, d, J = 21.2 Hz, CH2), 7.26-7.40 (5H, m, Ph); 19F (376MHz,
CDCl3): δ -91.76 (1F, m); 13C (Normal/DEPT-135): δ 23.34 (-ve, d, J =
31.0 Hz, CH2Br), 25.55 (-ve, d, J = 6.0 Hz, CH2Br), 115.22 (d, J = 19.0
Hz, C-2), 126.92 (+ve, ArCH), 128.48 (+ve, ArCH), 129.64 (+ve, ArCH),
130.85 (d, J = 3.0 Hz, ArC), 157.17 (d, J = 269 Hz, C-3); ν max (CHCl3)
(cm-1): 3058, 1643, 1582, 1477, 1260, 1216, 968, 742; GC-MS: m/z 340
(M+). Anal. Calcd: C, 35.32; H, 2.67. Found: C, 35.01; H, 2.54.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM yield depends on reaction conditions (amt. of reactant)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of 2-Fluoro-3-phenylthio-1,3-butadiene and
2-Trifluoromethyl-3-phenylthio-1,3-butadiene and Their Reactivities
toward Various Dienophiles
