$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: The One-Pot β-C-H Halogenation of Enones.
General Experimental Procedures for Compounds 20a, 31a-35a, 36, 37a, 38,
39a, 40-42, 43a-45a, and 46 . The enone (1.00 mmol, 1 equiv) was added to
a mixture of sodium sulfate (440 mg, 3.10 mmol, 3.10 equiv) and
tert-butyl carbazate (142 mg, 1.05 mmol, 1.05 equiv) in
1,2-dichloroethane (0.8 mL) in a pressure flask. The resulting suspension
was heated to 85 °C. After 4.5 h, the reaction mixture was allowed to
cool to 23 °C. Dichloromethane (3 mL) was added, the solution was cooled
to 0 °C, and recrystallized N-bromosuccinimide (187 mg, 1.05 mmol, 1.05
equiv) was added. After 1 h, triethylamine (292 μL, 2.10 mmol, 2.10
equiv) was added in one portion. The resulting suspension was allowed to
warm to 23 °C and was stirred at 23 °C until full consumption of the
intermediate allylic bromide (monitored by TLC) was observed.
Acetone-water (v/v = 9:2, 3.5 mL) and Amberlyst 15 (1.20 g) were added,
and the suspension was heated to 50 °C. After 14 h, the reaction mixture
was allowed to cool to 23 °C and then was diluted with dichloromethane (4
mL). The crude mixture was dried over sodium sulfate, the dried solution
was filtered, and the filtrate was concentrated. The residual oil was
purified by flash column chromatography on silica gel (ethyl
acetate/hexanes or diethyl ether/pentane) to afford the product. Methyl
2-Bromo-1-methyl-4-oxo-2-cyclohexene-1-carboxylate (34a). The general
procedure was followed, using methyl
1-methyl-4-oxo-2-cyclohexene-1-carboxylate (168 mg, 1.00 mmol), affording
34a after purification by flash column chromatography (6% ethyl acetate
in hexanes), A colorless oil (172 mg, 70%). TLC (25% ethyl acetate in
hexanes): R f = 0.53 (UV, Anis). 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 6.54 (s, 1H),
3.78 (s, 3H), 2.59-2.41 (m, 3H), 2.14-2.04 (m, 1H), 1.57 (s, 3H). 13C NMR
(100 MHz, CDCl3): δ 195.0, 172.9, 152.3, 133.9, 53.2, 51.1, 34.0, 24.0.
IR (Diamond-ATR, neat) v max : 2952 (w), 1733 (s), 1681 (s), 1602 (w),
1456 (w), 1291 (m), 1267 (m), 1251 (s), 1173 (s), 1115 (m) cm-1. HR-MS
(EI): calcd for (C9H11O3 79Br)+ 245.9892, found 245.9866.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, pressure flask used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Experimental Studies on the Selective β-C-H Halogenation of Enones
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Huber, Tatjana; Kaiser, Daniel; Rickmeier, Jens; Magauer, Thomas
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2015), 80(4), 2281-2294

