$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 7,8-Bis(bromomethyl)benzo[g]quinoline-5,10-dione (8) To a solution of
7,8-dimethylbenzo[g]quinoline-5,10-dione (7) (500 mg, 2.11 mmol) in
1,2-dichloroethane (50 mL) was added NBS (1.502 g, 8.44 mmol) and
benzoylperoxide (53 mg, 0.45 mmol). The reaction mixture was refluxed for
18 h under nitrogen atmosphere with the irradiation of W-lamp (60-70 W).
The solvent was evaporated in vacuo to dryness and the residue was
purified by flash column chromatography (CH2Cl2) to give the compound 8.
Yellow solid, yield 580 mg, 69.7 %. IR (KBr) 3032, 2978, 1689, 1195 cm-1;
1H NMR (acetone-d6, 300MHz) δ 9.33 (dd, J = 4.7 Hz, J = 1.7 Hz, 1 H,
hetAr-H), 8.90 (s, 1 H, Ar-H), 8.69 (dd, J = 7.9 Hz, J = 1.7 Hz, 1 H,
hetAr-H), 8.35 (s, 1 H, Ar-H), 7.93 (dd, J = 7.9 Hz, J = 4.7 Hz, 1 H,
hetAr-H), 4.90 (s, 4 H, CH2Br).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, W-lamp used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis and in Vitro cytotoxic activities of
2-alkyl-2,3-dihydro-1H-2,6-diazacyclopenta[b]anthracene-5,10-diones
