$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step a (Bromination): Pyridinium tribromide (40 mg, 0.12 mmol) was added
to a solution of 11c-R/S (62 mg, 0.083 mmol) in dioxane and the resulting
mixture was stirred at ambient temperature for 8 h. Volatiles were
evaporated and the residue was partitioned (NaHCO3//H2O/EtOAc). The
organic layer was washed (brine), dried (Na2SO4) and evaporated to give
crude 19 of sufficient purity for direct use in next step: Step b (Deh
ydrobromination): DBU (0.3 mL) was added to a solution of the crude 19 in
dried THF (3 mL) and the resulting mixture was stirred at room
temperature overnight. Volatiles were evaporated and the residue was
partitioned (NaHCO3//H2O/EtOAc). The organic layer was washed (brine),
dried (Na2SO4), evaporated and chromatographed (30 → 90% EtOAc/Hexane) to
give 20 {48 mg, 70% from 11c; MS m/z 903 (55%, MH+[81Br2]), 901 (100%,
MH+[81/79Br2]), 899 (50%, MH+[79Br2]). MS m/z 821 (100%, MH+[81Br], 819
(95%, MH+[79Br]} and the corresponding N 6 monobenzoylated product {12
mg, 20% from 11c; MS m/z 717 (100%, MH+[81Br]), 715 (95%, MH+[79Br]}.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
