$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of alkylnaphthazarines IIa-IIf
with molecular bromine in CCl4. General procedure. To a solution of 0.2
mmol of naphthazarine in 50 ml of CCl4 was added at room temperature 10
μl of Br2, and the reaction mixture was kept in light within 0.5-24 h. On
completion of the reaction the solvent was removed under a vacuum, the
residue was subjected to preparative TLC (eluent hexane-acetone, 3:1), or
it was recrystallized from ethanol.
2-(1'-Bromoethyl)-5,8-dihydroxy-6,7-dichloro-1,4-naphthoquinone (IIIc).
Yield 70%, golden-brown crystals. Time 0.5-1 hour, room temperature. mp
210-213°C (acetone). IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 2980, 1928, 1624 (C═O), 1576,
1564 (C═C). 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 2.03 d (3H, CH3, J 7.1 Hz), 5.55 q
(1H, H1', J 7.1 Hz), 7.52 s (1H, H3), 12.34 s, 12.94 s (2H, α-OH). Mass
spectrum, m/z (Irel, %): 364/366/368/370 [M]+ (27), 363/365/367/369
[M-1]+ (30), 285/287/289 [M - Br]+ (100), 284/286/288 [M - Br - H]+ (99),
256/ 258/260 (21), 255/257/259 (18). Found, %: C 39.68; H 2.02.
C12H7BrCl2O4. Calculated, %: C 39.38; H 1.93.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, regioselective, direct sun light used
