$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination with N-Bromosuccinimide/K-10;
α-Bromo β-Enamino Ketones 2a-g, 4a and α-Bromo β-Enamino Ester 4b;
General Procedure N-Bromosuccinimide (3.5 mmol) was suspended in MeOH (6
mL) and added to 3-amino-5,5-dimethylcyclohex-2-en-1-one 1a-g, 4-amino
penten-2-one 4a or ethyl 3-amino butenoate 3b (3 mmol) dispersed on K-10
(0.9 g; Fluka). The mixture was stirred at r.t. for 5 h. After completion
of the reactions (TLC/CH2Cl2), the products were extracted by washing the
K-10 with CH2Cl2 (4 10 mL). The combined organic layers were washed with
sat. NaHCO3 (13 mL), dried (MgSO4), filtered, and the solvent was removed
under vacuum to yield the crude products. Solid compounds were
recrystallized from diisopropyl ether. Compound 2d was purified by column
chromatography on silica gel (Aldrich, 230-400 mesh) using EtOAc-CH2Cl2
(1:1). Yields and NMR data are repoorted in the table. Compound 2e, yield
70%. Mp(°C): 158-159; 1H NMR (200 MHz, CDCl3) δ (ppm), J (Hz): 1.05 (s, 6
H), 2.43 (s, 2 H), 2.44 (s, 2 H), 7.12-7.43 (m, 5 H); 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3) δ (ppm): 27.91, 32.74, 41.40, 50.69, 96.75, 125.74, 126.85,
129.52, 137.28, 157.36, 188.15.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM montmorillonite K-10 catalyst
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM α-Bromination of β-enamino compounds using K-10
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Braibante, Mara E. F.; Braibante, Hugo T. S.; Rosso, Giovanni B.; Da
Roza, Juliano K.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2001), (13), 1935-1937

