$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Brominations with Pr4NBr9; General Procedure
A. A round-bottom flask equipped with a magnetic stir bar and a rub- ber
septum was charged with Pr4NBr9 (0.66 mmol, 0.33 mol%) and CH2Cl2 (1 mL).
The homogeneous solution was stirred and cooled to 0 °C if not described
otherwise (partial precipitation of the non- abromide can occur at this
point). The substrate (2.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv) was added and the reaction
allowed to warm to 23 °C (attention: exothermic reaction) After the
reported reaction time the dark-red color of the nonabromide had vanished
and TLC control showed completion of the reaction. The reaction was
quenched by addition of sat. aq Na2S2O3 (2 mL) and transferred to a
separation funnel. H2O was added (15 mL) followed by extraction with Et2O
(4 × 20 mL) if not described otherwise. The organic layers were combined,
washed with H2O (4 × 15 mL), dried (Na2SO4), filtered, and concentrated
under reduced pressure to give the crude product. Following general
procedure A, the reaction was quenched after 1 min. The product was
isolated after extraction with Et2O-H2O. (2,3-Dibromopropyl)benzene (14):
Yield: 88%, Product 15: Yield: 7%. Reagent: Br2, Equiv: 1.05, solvent:
CHCl3. Reactant: allylbenzene (13). 14: 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 3.15
(dd, J = 7.8, 14.5 Hz, 1 H), 3.53 (dd, J = 4.7, 14.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.65 (dd,
J = 8.9, 10.4 Hz, 1 H), 3.84 (dd, J = 4.2, 10.5 Hz, 1 H), 4.38 (dddd, J =
4.2, 4.8, 7.8, 8.9 Hz, 1 H), 7.28-7.40 (m, 5 H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM exothermic
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Brominations with Pr4NBr9 as a solid reagent with high reactivity and
selectivity
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Beck, Thorsten M.; Haller, Heike; Streuff, Jan; Riedel, Sebastian
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (2014), 46(6), 740-747, 8 pp.

