$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,1,3-Tribromo-2-(bromomethyl)prop-1-ene (2aa); Typical Procedure In a
250 mL three-necked flask, fitted with a stirrer, N2 inlet tube and
reflux condenser were placed 1,1-dibromo-2-methylprop-1-ene (3a;10 g,
0.0472 mol), N-bromosuccinimide (16.2 g, 0.092 mol), benzoyl peroxide
(1.7 g, 15 mol%) (Caution!),11 and CCl4 (100 mL). The mixture was stirred
at reflux under N2 for 2 h (The consumption of the starting material was
monitored by 1H NMR spectra). After filtration, the succinimide formed
was washed with CCl4 (2 × 30 mL). Rotary evaporation and flash
chromatography on silica gel (eluent: petroleum ether) afforded 2aa
2aa;Slightly yellowish solid, 15.0 g (86%),
1,1,3,3-Tetrabromo-2-(bromomethyl)prop-1-ene (2ac) 5%. 2aa; mp 46 °C. 1H
NMR: δ = 4.22 (s). IR (KBr): ν =1576, 1432, 1242, 1206, 1150 cm-1. MS:
m/z (%) = 376 [M+ (4 × 81Br), 2.75], 374 [M+ (3 × 81Br, 1 × 79Br),
11.54], 372 [M+ (2 × 81Br, 2 × 79Br), 17.38], 370 [M+ (1 × 81Br, 3 ×
79Br), 11.89], 368 [M+ (4 × 79Br), 3.59], 295 [M+ (3 × 81Br), 33.32], 293
[M+ (2 × 81Br, 1 × 79Br), 100.00], 291 [M+ (1 × 81Br, 2 × 79Br), 97.96],
289 [M+ (3 × 79Br), 33.88]. HRMS: m/z calcd for C4H4 79Br4 (M+):
367.7046. Found: 367.7058. Crystal data: C8H6Br10, M = 901.18, colorless
prismatic, space group Pï(#2), a = 9.774(4), b = 11.717(3), c = 8.391(2)
Å, α = 94.21(2)°, β = 97.06(3) °, γ = 85.29(2), V = 948.5(5) Å3, Z = 2,
Dc = 3.155 g/cm3, F(000) = 808.00. m(Mo-Kα) = 211.70 cm-1, Radiation:
MoKα (λ = 0.71069 Å). Crystal dimensions = 0.20×0.20×0.30 mm, R= 0.051,
Rw = 0.061, (Δρ)max = 1.04 and (Δρ)min = -1.12 e--/Å3.
1,1,3,3-Tetrabromo-2-(bromomethyl)prop-1-ene (2ac); 1H NMR: δ = 6.82(s, 1
H), 4.34 (s, 2 H). 13C NMR: δ = 138.44, 99.51, 38.60, 29.22. IR (KBr): ν
=1560, 1432, 1246, 1216, 1142 cm-1. MS: m/z (%) = 456 [M+ (5 × 81Br),
1.47], 454 [M+ (4 × 81Br, 1 × 79Br), 7.39], 452 [M+ (3 × 81Br, 2 × 79Br),
14.75], 450 [M+ (2 × 81Br, 3 × 79Br), 14.53], 448 [1 × 81Br, 4 × 79Br),
7.21], 446 [M+ (5 × 79Br), 1.49], 371 (100.00). Anal. calcd for C4H3Br5:
C, 10.66; H, 0.67. Found: C, 10.45; H, 0.54.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM product depends on stoichiometry
