$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Bromination of Methyl
2-Methylazulene-3-carboxylate (1) with NBS N-bromosuccinimide (106 mg,
0.6 mmol) was added to a solution of methyl 2-methylazulene-3-carboxylate
(1) (0.5 mmol) in benzene (20 ml). After stirring for 1 h at room
temperature. cold water (20 ml) was added to the mixture. The combined
organic layer and extracts were washed with water and dried over sodium
sulfate. The evaporation residue was chromatographed on a silica-gel
column with benzene as eluent. The blue fraction was collected and
afforded 1-bromo-2-methylazulenes 2. The reaction in a molar ratio of
1:2.2 under refluxing for 24 h in benzene afforded 2 in 11 % yield and
1-bromo-2-(bromomethyl)azulene (3) in 86% yield, respectively (entry 2).
Methyl 1-Bromo-2-methylazulene-3-carboxylate (2) 2: mp 88-89°C IR (KBr):
ν1694 (C=O) cm-1; 1H NMR (CDCl3): 82.77 (3H, s, CH3), 3.95 (3H, s,
COOCH3), 7.38 (1 H. dd, J = 9.9-9.6 Hz, 5- or 7-H), 7.42 (1H, dd, J=
10.2,9.9 Hz, 7- or 5-H), 7.64 (,H, t, J=9.9Hz, 6-H), 8.31 (1H, d,
J=9.9Hz, 8-H), 9.36 (1H, d, J=9.9Hz. 4-H); 13C NMR (CDCl3): 17.1 (CH3),
51.0 (COOCH3), 108.6 (=C<). 114.4 (=C<), 127.2 (=CH-), 128.1 (=CH-).
135.4 (=CH-), 136.6 (=CH-), 138.3 (=CH-), 140.6 (=C<). 151.1 (=C<), 165.7
(COOCH3). Anal. calcd. for C13H11BrO2: C, 55.94; H, 3.97%. Found: C,
56.19: H, 3.94%. 3: mp 99-101°C: IR (KBr): ν1679 (C=O) cm-1: 1H NMR
(CDCl3): δ 4.02 (3H, s, COOCH3). 5.17 (2H. s, CH2Br), 7.4g (1H, dd, J =
11.1,9.9 Hz. 5 or 7-H), 7.52 (1H. dd, J = 11.1,10.2 Hz, 7- or 5-H), 7.77
(1H. t, J = 9.9 Hz, 6-H), 8.46 (1H, d, J = 9.0 Hz, 8-H), 9.52 (1H, d, J =
9.9 Hz, 4-H); δC NMR (CDCl3): 26.4 (CH2Br), 51.5 (COOCH), 108.1 (=C<),
113.3 (=C<), 127.9 (=CH-), 128.8 (=CH-), 137.8 (=CH-), 138.8 (=C<), 139.0
(=CH-), 140.5 (=CH-), 140.7 (=C<), 146.9(=C< ), 164.9
(COOCH).Anal.Calcd.for C13H10Br2O2:C, 43.61: H. 2.81 %. Found: C. 43.52:
H. 2.81 %.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Methyl 2-methylazulene-3-carboxylate in the presence of
molecular sieves and reaction with N-bromosuccinimide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
