$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Cyclohexene→1,2-Dibromocyclohexene PA (0.42 mL, 0.15 g, 2.0 mmol) was
slowly added to a solution of TEABr (1.05 g, 5.00 mmol) in 10 mL of MeCN.
After stirring for 5 min, 0.041g of cyclohexene (0.50 mmol) was added.
The reaction mixture was analyzed by GC after stirring for 2 h at 22°C,
using chlorobenzene as an internal standard. The product was formed in
77% yield and was identified by GC/MS. A single side-product,
3-bromocyclohexene, was present in 23% yield.
