$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Compounds V-XIII. General procedure. To a
mixture of 0.1 mol of olefin and 80 mL of tetrachloromethane was added
NBS [0.105 (V, VIII, IX), 0.21 (VI, XII, XIII), 0.3 mol (VII)] and 1 mmol
of AIBN. The reaction mixture was refluxed at constant stirring for 3
(V), 5 (VI), 15 (VII, XII, XIII), and 20 h (VIII, IX). The succinimide
was filtered off, the filtrate was washed with 20 mL of water and dried
with anhydrous Na2SO4. Tetrachloromethane was evaporated on a rotary
evaporator in a vacuum. 2-(1-Adamantyl)-3-bromoprop-1-ene (VIII).
Reaction product was chromatographed on silica gel, eluent cyclohexane.
Yield 76%, light-yellow oil. (E)-2-(1-Adamantyl)-1-bromoprop-1-ene (IX).
Mixture of bromides VIII, IX was separated by column chromatography on
silica gel, eluent cyclohexane. Yield 38%, white crystals. VIII: IR
spectrum, ν, cm-1: 2904 (CHAd), 2848 (CHAd), 1626 (C═C), 1450 (CH2Ad),
1344, 1209, 1103, 908, 719, 665, 547. 1H NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.62-1.75
m (12H, 6CH2Ad ), 1.96- 2.06 m (3H, 3CHAd), 4.02 s (2H, CH2Br), 5.11 and
5.25, ═CH2). 13C NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 28.63, 36.79, 37.91, 38.46, 41.51,
115.81, 154.23. Mass spectrum, m/z (Irel, %): 254 (11)[M]+, 175 (100),
135 (42), 133 (12), 117 (17), 105 (13), 93 (23), 91 (25), 79 (21), 77
(15). Found, %: C 61.27; H 7.36. C13H19Br. Calculated, %: C 61.18; H
7.50. M 255.19. IX: mp 38-40°C. IR spectrum, ν, cm-1: 2910 (CHAd), 2848
(CHAd), 1604 (C═C), 1448 (CH2Ad), 1365, 1342, 1321, 1273, 1103, 1056,
977, 867, 767 (C-Br, trans), 725, 582, 532. 1H NMRspectrum, δ, ppm:
1.60-1.76 m (12H, 6CH2Ad), 1.77 d (3H, CH3, J 1.2 Hz), 1.98-2.07 m (3H,
3CHAd), 5.94 q (1H, ═CH, J 1.2 Hz). 13C NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 15.72,
28.57, 36.86, 39.89, 40.69, 102.48, 149.91. Mass spectrum, m/z (Irel, %):
254 (7)[M]+, 175 (100), 135 (53), 117 (23), 105 (15), 93 (35), 91 (41),
79 (41), 77 (25), 67 (19). Found, %: C 61.05; H 7.75. C13H19Br.
Calculated, %: C 61.18; H 7.50. M 255.19.
