$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM The chloroform solution of compound III was additionally treated with two
equivalents of bromine. After the solvent removal (12 mm Hg) a pale
orange oil was obtained, a mixture of VI and Z-isomer of
1-bromo-2-(3-bromo-2-hydroxy-5-chlorophenyl)-2-phenylethenyldiethyl-phosphine
oxide. Mixture of
3,8-dibromo-4-phenyl-6-chloro-2,2-diethylbenzo[e]-1,2-oxaphosphorin-2-onium
tribromide VI, yield 70% (δP 90.7 ppm) and Z-isomer of
1-bromo-2-(3-bromo-2-hydroxy-5-chlorophenyl)-2-phenylethenyldiethyl-phosphine
oxide, yield 24% (δP 70.6 ppm). 13C NMR spectrum, δC, ppm (J, Hz) for
compound VI: 96.68 d (d) (C3, 1JPC 87.2), 158.71 m (s)(C4), 123.58 d (d)
(C4a, 3JPCCC 10.9), 128.73 d.d (s) (C5, 1JHC 161.6, 3JHCCC 6.6), 125.65
br.s (s) (C6), 132.21 d.d(s) (C7, 1JHC7 171.4, 3JHCCC7 5.6), 114.47 br.d
(d) (C8, 3JPCCC8 5.7), 140.53 d.d.d (d) (C8a, 2JPCC8a 10.8, 3JHCCC8a 8.2,
3JHCCC8a 8.2), 133.59 m (d) (C9, 3JPCCC9 10.1), 19.39 d.t (d) C13, 1JHC13
127.6, 1JPC13 69.0), 5.92 d.q.m (br.d)(C14, 1JHC14 130.5, 2JPCC14 5.0).
13C NMR spectrum, δC, ppm (J, Hz) for compound VII: 111.15 d (d) (C3,
1JPC3 93.0), 159.79 m (s) (C4), 132.39 d.d (s) (C7, 1JHC7 171.0, 3JHC5CC7
5.5), 112.05 br.s (s) (C8), 146.60 d.d (s)(C8a, 3JHCCC8a 7.8, 3JHCCC8a
