$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Bromination of Cyclohexene (5) Using Ethyl
3-Bromo-2,4-dioxo-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroquinoline-3-carboxylate (4). A
mixture of the 3-bromo-substituted ester 4 (3.12 g, 0.01 mol),
cyclohexene freshly distilled over P2O5 (1.1 ml, 0.01 mol), and several
crystals of diperoxyazelaic acid in anhydrous CCl4 (15 ml) was refluxed
for 20 h. The product was cooled to room temperature and held at -25°C
for 1 day. The precipitated solid was filtered off and washed with a
small amount of cold CCl4. Crystallization from alcohol gave (8)
identified by the absence of a depression of melting point when mixed
with a known sample. Solvent and unreacted cyclohexene were distilled off
from the combined filtrates at about 100°C. The residue (0.76 g)
underwent chromato-mass spectrometric investigation. ethyl
4-hydroxy-2-oxo-1,2-dihydroquinoline-3-carboxylate (8), Yield 1.03 g, The
content of the 3-bromocyclohexene (6) was 11%. The content of
trans-1,2-dibromocyclohexane (7) was 78%. 6: Mass spectrum, m/z (Irel,
%): 160 [M]+ (2.6), 81[M-Br]+ (100), 65 (5), 53 (12). 7: Mass spectrum:
240[M]+ (4), 161[M-Br]+ (37), 81 (M-Br-Br)+ (100).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM stereoselective
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 4-hydroxy-2-quinolones. Part 125. Ethyl
3-bromo-2,4-dioxo-1,2,3,4-tetrahydroquinoline-3-carboxylates as potential
brominating agents
