$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of trimethyl(3-phenylpropoxy)silane with
N-bromohexamethyldisilazane. The equimolar mixture of 14.6 g (0.07 mol)
of trimethyl(3-phenylpropoxy) silane and 16.8 g (0.07 mol) of
N-bromo-hexamethyldisilazane was charged into a dry reaction tube,
degassed by the freezing/defreezing method, sealed and irradiated by the
UV light for 4 h. After distillation at atmospheric pressure
hexamethyldisiloxane, hexamethyldisilazane, and trimethylbromosilane was
obtained. Vacuum distillation gave
trimethyl(3-bromo-2-phenylpropoxy)silane. Yield 3.8 g, 46%; Yield 9.2 g,
82%; Yield 0.1 g, 0.5%; Yield 7.1 g, 35%. hexamethyldisiloxane: bp 100°С,
nD20 1.3774 bp 123°С (2 mm Hg), nD22 = 1.5062; 1Н NMR (δ, ppm): 0.17 s
(9Н, Ме3Si); 2.44-2.27 m (2Н, -СН2-); 2.52-2.48 m (2Н, СН2Ph); 5.74-5.71
m (1Н, -СНBr); 7.58-7.13 m (5Н, С6Н5).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, sealed ampoule used, equimolar mixture of reactants used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Homolytic reactions of N-bromohexamethyldisilazane with
trialkyl(phenylalkoxy) derivatives of silicon and tin
