$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Reaction of trimethyl(phenethyloxy)silane with
N-bromohexamethyldisilazane. The equimolar mixture of 13.6 g (0.07 mol)
of trimethyl(phenethyloxy)silane and 16.8 g (0.07 mol) of
N-bromohexamethyl-disilazane was charged into a dry reaction tube,
degassed by the freezing/defreezing method, sealed and irradiated by the
UV light for 6 h. After distillation at atmospheric pressure
hexamethyldisiloxane, hexamethyldisilazane, and trimethylbromosilane was
obtained. Vacuum distillation gave
trimethyl(2-bromo-2-phenylethoxy)silane. Yield 2.6 g, 31%; Yield 8.2 g,
72%; Yield 1.1 g, 10%; Yield 6.9 g, 36%. hexamethyldisiloxane: bp 100°С,
nD20 1.3774 bp 167°С (3 mm Hg); 1Н NMR (δ, ppm): 0.1 s (9Н, Ме3Si);
4.15-4.02 t (2Н, -СН2-); 4.99-4.95 m (1Н, -СНBr-); 7.57-7.23 m (5Н,
С6Н5).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM photochemical, sealed ampoule used, equimolar mixture of reactants used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Homolytic reactions of N-bromohexamethyldisilazane with
trialkyl(phenylalkoxy) derivatives of silicon and tin
