$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure of Drim-8(9)-en-7-one 2 Bromination. A calculated
quantity of NBS was added to a solution of drimenone 2 (1 mmol) in dry
CCl4 (15 mL) (entries a-c, Table 2). The resulting mixture was refluxed
for 3 h, and after each hour the reaction was monitored by the GC-MS
method. After cooling, the reaction products were filtered and the
solvent removed in vacuo. The crude reaction products were purified by
column chromatography on SiO2 (eluant: EP/EtOAc in increasing gradients)
to give major reaction compounds 10, 16, and 19 in the mentioned yields
(Table 2) and several minor compounds 17, 18, and 20, as follows.
11-Bromo-drim-8-tn-7-one 10 as white crystals (from EP),
11,12-Dibromo-drim-8-tn-7-one 16 as white crystals (from EP),
6,11,12-tribromo-drim-8-tn-7-one 17, unstable as white crystals,
11,12-dibromo-drim-5,8(9)-ditn-7-one 18 as white crystals (from EP),
12-Bromo-drim-8-tn-7-one 19, unstable; 11-bromo-drim-5,8(9)-ditn-7-one
20, unstable. 10: mp 105-107 °C (from EP), [α]D25 +135.1 - (c 18.2); IR
νmax (film): 3370, 3070, 2850, 1608, 1446, 1362, 1090, 1028, 893, 721
cm-1; 1H NMR (400.13 MHz) δH: 4.09 (1H, d, J 9.8 Hz) and 4.03 [1H, d, J
9.8 Hz, C(11)-H2], 2.52 (1H, d, J 3.8, 14.3 Hz) and 2.36 [1H, dd, J 3.8,
14.3 Hz, C(6)-H2], 1.84 [3H, s, C(12)-H3], 1.14 [3H, s, C(15)-H3], 0.91
[3H, s, C(13)-H3], 0.87 [3H, s, C(14)-H3]. 13C NMR (100.64 MHz) δC: 199.8
(C-7), 159.9 (C-9), 134.3 (C-8), 50.2 (C-5), 41.1 (C-3), 40.3 (C-10),
35.5 (C-1), 35.2 (C-11), 32.7 (C-4), 32.3 (C-14), 26.3 (C-6), 21.2
(C-13), 18.9 (C-15), 18.4 (C-2), 11.1 (C-12); m/z 299 (M+, 9), 283 (7),
218 (59), 203 (17), 177 (86), 163 (15), 149 (21), 137 (19), 123 (36), 105
(23), 95 (32), 83 (23), 69 (87), 55 (66), 41 (100), HRMS (EI): found
299.09286; C15H23BrO requires 299.09323. 16: mp 107-108 °C. 18: mp
136-137 °C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, optimized on reagent amount and reaction time to achieve
the highest regioselectivity, 1.5 eq. NBS used, further increasing of NBS
amount or reaction time raise the yield of dibromide (99% using 2 eq.
NBS/3h), optimization study, controlled bromination
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of Polyfunctional Drimanes from Drim-7,9(11)-diene and
Drim-8-en-7-one
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
